Add the mm39 (GRCm39) genome to SICER's chromosome tables.

SICER resolves a `--species` argument by looking it up in `species_chroms`
and `species_chrom_lengths` in `sicer/lib/GenomeData.py`, and rejects
anything absent from both. Those tables stop at mm10, so mm39 -- UCSC's
current mouse assembly since 2020 -- cannot be used with this package at
all.

The patch is data only. It adds `mm39_chroms` (the 22 canonical
chromosomes, mirroring the mm10 entry directly above it),
`mm39_chrom_lengths`, and one registry entry each in `species_chroms` and
`species_chrom_lengths`. No code path is modified and no existing genome
is touched -- every lookup is keyed by species, so results for hg38, mm10
and the rest are unchanged.

The chromosome sizes are UCSC's mm39 values, taken from
https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/mm39/bigZips/mm39.chrom.sizes
and re-checked against the UCSC REST API
(https://api.genome.ucsc.edu/list/chromosomes?genome=mm39): all 22 match
exactly.

Precedent in this repository: `recipes/sicer/` has carried
`genome_additions_v1.patch` since it was created -- the same kind of
addition, to the same file, of the same project's 1.1 release, for mm10,
rn5 and rn6.

Offered upstream as https://github.com/tmx1228/SICER2.1.0/pull/1, open
since 2026-06-15 with no maintainer response. This recipe already builds
from tmx1228/SICER2.1.0, the maintained line of SICER2 (zanglab/SICER2
has not released since 1.0.3).

Correctness is checked by bioconda's own CI: the `test: commands:` entry
added to meta.yaml in the same commit asserts that mm39 is registered in
both tables and that its chr1 length is UCSC's value. Stock 2.1.0 fails
that assertion, so the test proves the patch is present in every shipped
artifact.

